00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,845
Meet FrontDesk, a patient access prototype for a synthetic clinic. This walkthrough
shows a working scheduling flow,

2
00:00:06,845 --> 00:00:10,871
a traceable tool audit, and clear boundaries around clinical questions.

3
00:00:11,571 --> 00:00:18,859
The staff dashboard brings conversations, appointments, refill requests, and handoffs
together. It is built with React and

4
00:00:18,859 --> 00:00:22,717
TypeScript, with a responsive layout for desktop and mobile.

5
00:00:23,417 --> 00:00:29,623
A patient starts by requesting an appointment. Before revealing patient information or
taking action, FrontDesk asks for

6
00:00:29,623 --> 00:00:34,734
a full name and date of birth. Here, we use the synthetic demo identity.

7
00:00:35,433 --> 00:00:42,371
After verification, the patient sees available slots with an exact date, time, and provider.
Choosing a slot

8
00:00:42,371 --> 00:00:45,635
moves the conversation to a separate confirmation step.

9
00:00:46,335 --> 00:00:53,055
FrontDesk repeats the appointment details and waits for confirmation. This separates a
suggested action from an executed

10
00:00:53,055 --> 00:00:55,427
action, keeping the patient in control.

11
00:00:56,127 --> 00:01:02,282
Once confirmed, the appointment is added and the dashboard updates. This is a
working browser simulation, with

12
00:01:02,282 --> 00:01:06,265
state saved on the device, rather than a static interface mockup.

13
00:01:06,965 --> 00:01:13,424
Staff can inspect the ordered tool calls: patient lookup, identity verification, slot search,
and booking. The trace

14
00:01:13,424 --> 00:01:19,123
makes it possible to see what the assistant actually did, not just what it said.

15
00:01:19,823 --> 00:01:27,125
The demo also includes guardrails. Recognized emergency language interrupts the
workflow. Two failed identity attempts trigger a

16
00:01:27,125 --> 00:01:34,428
staff handoff. Refill requests go to a review queue and are never automatically
approved. Handoffs are simulated

17
00:01:34,428 --> 00:01:34,858
records.

18
00:01:35,558 --> 00:01:43,761
The project includes a connected local Python API using FastAPI, Pydantic, and
SQLite. Forty Python checks and

19
00:01:43,761 --> 00:01:51,963
eight browser engine checks pass locally. They cover workflow completion, identity
guards, emergency interruption, and slot conflicts.

